      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-01-07_WidnesExaminer_art0007" n="art0007">
        <p>THE PUBLIC HEALTH ACT, 1875, AND THE PUBLIC HEALTH (SHIPS, Scc.) ACT, 1885. PORTS OF LIVERPOOL &amp; RUNCORN. WHEREAS by Section 287 of the Public Health Act, 1875, as amended by Section 3 of the Public Health (Ships, Isc.) Act. 1885, the Local Government Board may by Order permanently constitute any Sanitary Authority whose District, or part of whose District, forms part of, or abuts on any part of, a Port established for the purposes of the laws relating to the Customs of the United Kingdom, or the Waters of such Port, the Sanitary Authority of the whole of such Port. or any part thereof, or may by such Order permanently coustitute a Port Sanitary Authority by forming a Joint Board, consisting of representative Members of any Iwo or more Riparian Auth- orities having jurisdiction within the Port, or any part thereof, or may by such Order permanently constitute a Port Sanitary Authority for two or more Ports by forming a Joint Board consisting of representative members of all or any of the Riparian Authorities having jurisdiction within such Ports, or any part thereof. AND WHEREAS the Local Government Board may by such Order as aforesaid assign to the Port Sanitary Authority any powers, rights, duties, capacities, liabilities, and obliga- tions under the said Acts, direct the mode In which the expenses of such Port Sanitary Authority are to be paid, and if a Joint Board is formed may make regulations as to the qualification and mode of election of Members of such Joint Board, as to their continuance in office, as to their Meetings and officers, as to other matters and things. AND WHEREAS the Town Council of the City of Liver- pool, the Town Councils of the Boroughs of Birkenhead, Bootle, Southport, 1,4 trines, and Warrington, the Local Boards of the Districts of Wallasey, Lower Bebington, Bromborough, Garston, Toxteth Park, Great Crosby, Waterloo-with-Seaforth, Little Crosby, Birkdale, Iloylake and West Xirkby and Northwich, the Rnncorn Improvement Commissioners, and the Rural Sanitary Authorities of the Wirral], Chester,Pressot, Ormskirk, Runcorn, Northwich and Warrington Unions, are Riparian Authorities having jurisdic- tion within the said Ports of Liverpool and Runcorn or some part thereof. AND WHEREAS by a Provisional Order which was con- firmed by the Local Government Board's Provisional Orders Confirmation Act, 1874 (No. 4) the Town Council of the City of Liverpool were permanently constituted the Port Sanitary Authority for the whole of the Port of Liverpool, together with the waters of the said Port. AND WHEREAS the said Provisional Order was partly repealed and amended by a Provisional Order which was confirmed by the Local Government Board's Provisional Orders Confirmation (Aberdare) Act, 1875. AND WHEREAS it is proposed that a Provisional Order should be Issued for the repeal or alteration of the said Provisional Orders and that an Order under the enactments firstly hereinbefore recited should be made for the constite- tion of a Joint Board as the Port Sanitary Authority having jurisdiction within the said Ports or some parts thereof ; or that such other provision as may be authorised by the said enactments should be made for the Sanitary administration of the said Ports or some parts thereof, NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that Herbert Jenner-Fust, liCsq , and Frederick Wm. Barry Esq.. M.D. Inspectors of the said Board, will open a Local Inquiry into the subject- matter of the said Proposal and the other matters aforesai,t at the Council Chamber, Town Hall. Liver; 001, on Wednesday. the Eighteenth day of January, 1893, at half-past ten o'clock in the forenoon, and will continue the said Inquiry at such places, on such dates, and at such times as the said Inspec- tors may appoint. AND NOTICE IS HEREBY FURTHER GIVEN that any person interested may attend at such inquiry, and be heard with reference to the said proposal and the other</p>
        <p>- - . mattera aforesaid. AS WITNESS my hand this Third day of January, 1893, 'at the office of the Local government Board, Whitehall, Lon- don.</p>
        <p>ALFRED D. ADRIAN, Aseißtant Secretary.</p>
      </div>
