        <p>CEMETHRY COMItITTNE. Councillor HIITCHINBOX moved the adoption of the minutes of this Committee, which were of the usual fo</p>
        <p>Irmal character. Councillor Mune seconded. Councillor RoIERTS said that on calling that day at the lodge of the registrar at the Cemetery, he was per- fectly shocked to And that the room in which the busi- ness of the registrar was transacted was as full of sewer gas as it could be, and the registrar's married daughter, who lived there, told him that had been the ease there for some time ; and if they did not loss valuable life through it he should be very much surprised. Never in his life had he been so impressed with the density of an odour as he had with that of the stench which prevailed in that little room that afternoon. He had smelt sewer gas before, but never in such a quantity as there, and he directed publie attention to the matter, because he thought it so urgent that not five minutes unavoidable delay should occur in dealing with it. , The MAYOR said instructions would be given through ' the Town Clerk, to the Surveyor to attend to the</p>
        <p>LIVELY MEETING.</p>
        <p>The monthly meeting of the Town Council was keld at the Town Hall on Tuesday evening. 112 era were then present :—The Mayor (Alderman Wreenall), the Deputy Mayor (Alderman Fran- ca:oh), Aldermen G. Blackhurst, C. J. Holmes, T. H. ‘atton, J. E. Wright; Councillors J. Ashton, S. J. geaman, W. Bolton, J. Hormel], A. Browne, J. Can- ell. F. Dixon, IL T. Fairclough, J. Fairclough, T. I°lood, .J. H. Fleming, J. S. Green, R. Heaton, J. Ilep- T. Hutchinson, F. W. Monks, J. Muir, G. Plumpten, IL Roberts, W. J. Shaw, J. Smethurat, W. Tinsley, J. L. Whittle (town clerk) ; J. H. Gor- viall (medical officer).</p>
