        <p>WATCH AND TDIANCE COMMITTEES. The minutes of the Watch Committee,which contained thing of note, were adcpted, as were also those of the i'Mance Committee, which contained the following:— Orders were also made for payment of interest cut the boad debt amounting, to £1,760 13s. 9d.; also £4,598 Is. 9d., the half-year's water annuities and interest, and ,117 17s. 9d., the half-year's gas annuities and in- due 31st December, 1892.</p>
        <p>...... TOWN HALL, PARK, AND BATHS COMMITTEN. Thifil Committee recommended that the Borough Sur- veyor be empowered to engage a bricklayer as clerk of works during the construction of the new baths. Councillor Bovrom moved the adoption of the</p>
