        <p>On Saturday afternoon, a numerously attended meet- ing of delegates from all the polling districts in tie Par- liamentary division was held at Hexham. Mr. Miles M'lnnes, of rhickerhy ifouse, Carlisle, was unanim- ously selected as the Liberal candidate at the forthce-p- -ing -election, caused through the unseating. of Mr. Nathaniel G. Clayton on petition. QUITS TRUE Sufferers from Gravel, Lumbago, Piles, Pains in the Back, Dropsy, Wind and Water Complaints. Diseases of Kidneys, Bladder, Urinary Organs, Stone, Gleet, Stric- ture, Sciatica, Rheumatism, and Gout, will find a positive cure in Holdroyd's Gravel Pills. Try a small box, and if not satisfiedyour money will be returned. Prise Is 10. Of all chemists, or post free for 12 stamps from HOLD- BOYD'S Medical Hall, Cleckheaton, Yorks. Don't be put off. If you cannot get them write to the Proprietor, and a box will be sent aext post.—Advt. KAY'S COMPOUND Essence of Linseed, Aniseed, Senega, Squill, Tolu, Ac., 41. 13d., Lss. Of all Chemists.—Advt.</p>
