        <p>LONDON' PRoDUOR, FRIDAY—Sugar; Pieces, t OVA goods and crystals quiet butsteady ; foreign refined quiet; beet rather easier—January quo ed 14s 3ld and March 14s 51.; cane quiet. Coffee on the spot quiet ; auctions withdrawn owing to fog; futures steady ; Rio, March 7n3 and May 753 9fl• Tea quiet. Rice dull. Jute quiet. Linseed oil 193 jdt° 19s 4fd ; rape oil 233 3d. Turpentine, 223 3d. Americ.an petroleum, 40 to 41d spot.</p>
        <p>MANCHESTER TRADE, FRIDAY.—The market is strorl but not active, and the quantity of workable business off( ing seems to get less. Cotton, however, is in sornewils4 better form. Futures have gained a little since the openinet and the estimate of spot transactions has be n raised fr° 8,000 to 10,000 bales at hardenin4 prices. Yarns are ve' r,., strong, but there is only a very moderate trade gel" through. Only very moderate trade is doing to-day in either twist or weft. Bundles are slow, but some little business has changed hands in Egyptian qualities for Madras. Cloth Is no better. There is moderate inquiry for some Soutli American cloths, but for the smaller outlets generallf demand is not brisk. The small China inquiry at low Price°, is not quite satisfied. Workable offers for India fabrics be fallen off considerably, and the home inquiry is seldom large lines. LIVERPOOL PRODUCE, FRIDAY.—Cane Suar is stead/ but quiet, and so far no sales have been reported Beet Is quiet, January 143 3d value, February 14s slid, and Mere'. 14s 50, sellers. Molasses : There is little doing in America,' Treacle, and prices are unchanged from last week. RUM very quiet and the basiness concluded is at easier rate African Coffee continues firm, and 150 bags hold her; al.,' 4 to arrive at 4-6 s 6d per cwt., in transit, Cocoa is also.firin": tone, and 478 bags fermented Bahia sold at 66s per Cio Rice continues very quiet on the spot, but there is a little_ mere inquiry for arrival parcels at the /ow prices now current. There is only a small bus ness doing in Sago FRI at unchanged prices. Linseed is firm on spoi., but in vieW °t arrivals buyers hold off; 550 bags inferior Bombay sold 'ls 38s per 4161b5. Manilla Hemp is better; distant carrel), steady at £27 per ton c.i.f. terms. Lard is again dester,.: 54s 9d to 55s per cwt now asked, Tallow continues firm tone, but business is only small. Spirits of Torpentille. steas' at 22s 6d per cw.;. Refloed Petroleum is in good' suoipzlvs d