        <p>LATEST NE WS. AN IRON CHAIN SWALLOWED BY AN ELEPHANT. BARABOO, WISCONSIN, FRIDAY—On an autopsy being made upon Zip, a big elephant that died here recently, the stomach was found to contain an iron chain, four feet bug, which weighed ninety pounds. A BOY DEVOURED BY A WOLF. --- BITDAPESTR, TRIIRSDAX.—For several weeks intensely , severe weather has prevailed throughout Hungary. Violent snowstorms have been general, and during a heavy downfall to-day a wolf entered a suburb of this city and attacked and devoured a little fellow, four years old, outside his parents' house. THE PANAMA SCANDAL. MORE WARRANTS ISSUED. PARIS, FRIDAY.—The Petit Parisien says that yester- day evening a certain number of commissaries of police were summoned by the Public Prosecutor, who, it is said, handed them several warrants. It is expected that other arrests will be effected this morning. EX-HANGMAN BERRY ASSAULTED. Three men were charged at Edinburgh Police Court yesterday, with assaulting James Berry, the ex-haag- man, who is delivering a series of lectures in that city. The men were drinking with Berry at a bar on Thurs- day night when one of them quarrelled with Berry slid knocked him down. Berry left the bar, and was fol- lowed by the three others who, it is alleged, assaulted him in the street.</p>
